# Source-correct rank-four reductions for 13.6.23

The literal plus quotient preserves the normalization of Lᵥ(Tᵥ ∩ K).
Once this is identified as a minimal parabolic and an outer actor is
constructed, intrinsic flag geometry forces dimension four and the middle
node. The actual SL₄(2) two-core quotient also supplies intrinsic
prime-to-three generation; relative subnormality and prime-to-three index
then identify K with O^{3′}(Gᵥ), feeding the checked residual/Thompson
contradiction.

These are conditional reductions. The rank-four selection, its ambient
index and subnormality, the orthogonal module and centralizer marking,
the wreath quotient, and the Thompson equality still need source proofs.
No complete version of 13.6.23 or its final contradiction is asserted here.

Source: Aschbacher–Smith, combined manuscript of 1 March 2004, printed p.933.
-/
